{"kind":"assert","text":"Cutover head (05d618e2): rulings 190b31f4 are in, at e941e81d.\n- Q-S4: RETIRED_ROOM_READER_COMMIT lives in packages/bytes (src/retired-room.ts). Of the packages that scope and mcp both depend on, bytes is the lowest after contract. The value is 40 zeros, marked FILLED AT LANDING. The store-format refusal returns a plain Said.\n- Q-GP (a): genesis-proof.ts admits an entry by body and use digest, and adds no read. The exported helper is now bodyAndDigestProofEntry, and its comment says it proves body and digest, not an address.\n- Census: Config is v: 2. A v: 1 home raises RetiredHomeError before any command runs, `dap mcp` included.\n- 10(b): partitionIndexes already returns the partition references. The page keeps them, so a partition row locks the directory again and reads \"in this room\".\n- V1 and the ruling 9 seeds needed no change.\nSource configs compile with 0 errors for bytes, scope, mcp, cli and the room page. All the test configs compile clean except cli, platform and scope, which are in progress. No test has run.\n\nQuestions:\nP1. The room page stores the cli Config type inside its browser custody records: claim.ts, connection-custody.ts and oauth-custody.ts. The lane moved those to v: 2, so a browser record saved before the cutover no longer reads. Does item 6 cover that, or should the page keep its own config version?\nT1. Codec and transport tests use textDigest(\"TEST … genesis …\") as a stand-in genesis digest, as existing scope and replay tests already do. Is that allowed under ruling 9, which permits seeds and forbids a made-up genesis in place of an admitted one?\nT2. checkers does not depend on dap-derive, so its stage fixture writes its own genesis bytes and admits them with admitSequenceGenesis. Accept that, or add dap-derive as a dev dependency of checkers and use scriptedSequence?\nT3. Four held test assertions:\n  (a) replay/test/verify.test.ts checks a `covered.scope.kind` column in its coverage rows. What replaces that column: the genesis kind, or nothing?\n  (b) The same file expects /wrong incarnation/. I will set it to the new refusal text when the test first runs.\n  (c) checkers/test/fixtures/reservation-record.json is a frozen recording that still uses `at` and `inc`. It needs a new recording from the Scope recorder. May the head re-record it?\n  (d) mcp/test/room.scope.test.ts passes the hold `task` field as `{ ...laneRef, kind: \"task\" }`. Should that field now be the plain lane reference, the scope and genesis without a kind?\nUnless you rule otherwise: (a) drop the column, (b) as stated, (c) re-record, (d) the plain reference."}